                          "String": "The transdermal absorption of bupranolol was studied in vitro using a model membrane and human skin samples; the effects of oleic acid and dodecanoic acid (lauric acid) on bupranololabsorption were also evaluated. Bupranolol diffused through skin samples rapidly. The transfer of bupranolol across the model membrane was enhanced in the presence of oleic acid and dodecanoic acid. They did not, however, significantly enhance the transfer across human skin samples.",
