                          "String": "RURAL/REMOTE: Dodecanoic acid was qualitatively identified in air samples from a 45 year old spruce forest in Germany on January 11, 1988 at a height of 1 m(1). Dodecanoic acid was found on aerosols obtained over Chacaltaya, Bolivia with a mean concn of 1.6 ng/cu m(2). The average ambient concn was reported to be 0.5-10.3 ng/cu-m for dodecanoic acid(3). Dodecanoic acid was found in 32% of samples taken near a lighthouse in Fajardo and was also detected in the open ocean off the south coast of Puerto Rico(4). Atmospheric samples taken Dec 26-28, 1995 and Jan 4-6, 1996 in Kern Wildlife Refuge, CA had 0.812 and 0.660 ng/cu m of dodecanoic acid(5). The average ambient annual concn of dodecanoic acid in fine particles collected from San Nicolas Island , CA in 1982 was 0.19 ng/cu m(6). Dodecanoic acid was found at 4.8 ng/cu m from Sonnblick Observatory, Austria in samples taken May 1997(7). Dodecanoic acid was measured in the gas form at 0.90, 0.71 and 0.31 ng/cu m and in the aerosol form at 0.40, 0.78, and 1.24 ng/cu m at 6AM to 12PM, 12PM to 6PM, and 6PM to 6AM, respectively, in samples taken July 27 to August 8, 1998 in the Pertouli area of the Agrafa Mountains, Greece(8).",
